    "note": "The crimson Red Palace and five gilt roof pavilions rise above the white retaining walls and east and west wings. Three stepped exterior routes follow the southern hill. An open White Palace court is edged by timber galleries and a tiered ceremonial entrance. The 3,700 m sea-level datum uses standard viewer terrain. Battered foundations extend into the sampled hill. The cutout replaces the named palace footprint and retains the independent buildings and paths around it. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
